# Sendust example configuration.
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env`:
#
#        cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Replace every placeholder. The examples refuse values that still contain
#    `example.com`, `your-name`, or `your-16-char-app-password`, so an unedited
#    copy cannot send anything.
#
# 3. `.env` is git-ignored. Never commit real credentials. Real environment
#    variables win over this file.
#
# Keep exactly one relay profile below and comment out the other.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relay: Gmail (App Password)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Gmail rejects your normal account password here. Create an app password:
#
#        https://myaccount.google.com/security/apppasswords
#
# Google shows it as four groups, for example `abcd efgh ijkl mnop`. Remove the
# spaces before pasting: `abcdefghijklmnop`. The examples also strip them for a
# gmail.com relay and print a note when they do.
#
# SENDUST_USER and SENDUST_PASS must both be set or both be empty. For Gmail,
# SENDUST_FROM must be that same address (or an alias you own), otherwise Gmail
# rewrites or rejects the sender envelope.
SENDUST_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SENDUST_PORT=465
SENDUST_SECURITY=tls
SENDUST_USER=your-name@gmail.com
SENDUST_PASS=your-16-char-app-password

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relay: any other SMTP relay (comment out the Gmail lines above first)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `tls` is implicit TLS and is usually port 465. `starttls` connects in
# plaintext, requires the STARTTLS extension, and upgrades; it is usually 587.
# Verification is always on: a relay with a self-signed certificate fails unless
# you add its PEM anchor with SENDUST_EXTRA_ROOT.
# SENDUST_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SENDUST_PORT=587
# SENDUST_SECURITY=starttls
# SENDUST_USER=
# SENDUST_PASS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Message
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SENDUST_TO is a comma-separated list. The From address is the envelope sender;
# the relay may require it to match the authenticated account.
SENDUST_FROM="Sendust Test <your-name@gmail.com>"
SENDUST_TO=your-name@gmail.com
SENDUST_SUBJECT=Hello from Sendust
SENDUST_TEXT=Sent by the Sendust example.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rust example only: extra PEM trust anchor for a local test relay.
# SENDUST_EXTRA_ROOT=tests/fixtures/tls/ca.crt
